Phase 1: System Initialization & Configuration

Fleet & Operational Parameter Setup:

 Configure hard operational constraints: maximum payload (2.0 kg), cruise velocity (65 km/h), maximum flight duration (55 min), and safety thresholds (wind limit ≤30 km/h, precipitation flag =0).

   Set drop-off service duration (default: 2 min per delivery).

API Credential & Endpoint Maintenance: Verify API tokens and quotas for Google Geocoding, Distance Matrix, Roads APIs, and OpenWeatherMap/Open-Meteo services.

Geofence & Restricted Airspace Configuration: Upload and update GeoJSON/shapefile polygons designating No-Fly Zones (NFZs), military airbases, and high-security installations.

Phase 2: Order Ingestion & Airspace Triage Management

 Batch Ingestion: Upload customer order batches (addresses, parcel weights, delivery priority) via CSV or automated API endpoints.

 Automated Airspace Triage Review: Monitor the spatial boundary validation engine.

 Review orders flagged inside restricted zones and verify automated handoff to the third-party ground logistics platform.

 Geocode Validation & Manual Resolution: Resolve unmatched, ambiguous, or out-of-boundary delivery addresses flagged during preprocessing.
 

Phase 3: Model Execution & Route Authorization

  Pre-Flight Optimization Review: Ingest the dynamic cost matrix generated from the LSTM Weather Forecaster and MLP Energy Surrogate.
          Inspect the clustered delivery routes and stop sequences generated by the Attention-Based Graph Neural Network (GNN).

  Feasibility & Constraint Verification:

        Confirm that each scheduled drone cluster strictly respects the ≤2 kg payload limit.

        Verify that calculated round-trip durations (including 2-minute drop times) do not exceed the 55 min battery threshold.

    Mission Dispatch: Authorize and transmit optimized waypoint trajectories to the physical UAV fleet or simulation engine.

Phase 4: Live Fleet Tracking & Real-Time Monitoring

    Telemetry Oversight: Track real-time UAV states via the Mission Control Dashboard:  Drone GPS coordinates and snapped polyline path.

        Instantaneous ground speed and altitude.

        State of Charge (SOC) / remaining battery percentage.

        Localized live wind speeds and precipitation readings along active flight vectors.

    Threshold Monitoring: Monitor automated status indicators (Green: Nominal, Amber: Weather Approaching Safety Limits, Red: Critical Constraint Violation).

Phase 5: Dynamic Re-Dispatch & Manual Overrides

    Automated Alert Handling: Review automated system actions triggered during flight disruptions:

        Rain / Wind >30 km/h Trigger: System commands mid-air hover/hold or issues immediate Return-to-Base (RTB).

        Excess Battery Depletion Trigger: Reinforcement Learning policy re-sequences remaining waypoints or reroutes directly to the nearest charging depot.

    Manual Override Intervention:

        Override automated decisions with direct fleet commands: Emergency Land, Return to Base (RTB), Hold Position, or Bypass Waypoint.

Phase 6: Post-Mission Analytics & ML Model Operations (MLOps)

    Telemetry Logging & Database Audit: Ingest finalized flight telemetry, actual energy consumption, and completed delivery timestamps into the central data lake (DuckDB).

    Cost & Performance Reporting:

        Generate ablation and savings reports comparing naive route baselines against deep learning-optimized schedules.

        Compute final metrics: average ETA reduction, mission completion rate, and cost per delivered package.

    Model Performance & Calibration:

        Compare predicted energy consumption (E^) from the MLP surrogate against actual flight power draw to detect prediction drift (R2, RMSE).

        Trigger model retraining or fine-tuning pipelines when prediction error margins exceed defined limits.

